This project is an independent implementation.

The design of the physics layer is *inspired by* the problem space explored by
Sable (https://github.com/ryanhcode/sable) and its Fabric port sable-port --
namely, rigid-body simulation of moving block structures built from voxel
collision shapes. No source code, comment text, or resource file from Sable or
sable-port was copied into this repository. A small number of public API names,
package structures and terms are intentionally aligned with Sable for migration
and compatibility (for example ForceGroup, MassData, RigidBodyHandle,
PhysicsPipeline, constraint configurations and VoxelColliderData). Their
implementations are independent.

sable-port and Crythst are maintained by the same author (mikaple). This
explains the intentional API/term alignment, but it does not change the
PolyForm Shield terms that apply to upstream Sable code; Crythst still contains
no copied Sable or sable-port source, comments, or resources.
Ideas, public Minecraft/Fabric APIs, and general physics techniques (greedy
voxel meshing, compound colliders, fixed-timestep integration, interpolated
rendering poses) were implemented from scratch.

